{"id":"leetcode-867","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Transpose Matrix","summary":"Given a 2D integer array matrix, return a new matrix where the rows become columns and vice versa.","statement":"Given a 2D integer array matrix, return a new matrix where the rows become columns and vice versa.","constraints":["Matrix is nonempty and rectangular.","Return its transpose, swapping rows with columns."],"topics":["matrices"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"transpose_matrix","parameters":[{"name":"matrix","annotation":"list[list[int]]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"list[list[int]]","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def transpose_matrix(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def transpose_matrix(matrix):\n return [[matrix[r][c] for r in range(len(matrix))] for c in range(len(matrix[0]))]\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def transpose_matrix(matrix):\n    return [row[:] for row in matrix]\n","def transpose_matrix(matrix):\n    return [list(reversed(row)) for row in matrix]\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(rows*columns)","target_space_complexity":"O(rows*columns)","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["Transposition maps output[c][r] to input[r][c].","Build one output row for each input column.","For c over columns, collect matrix[r][c] over rows.","Every input cell appears once at its coordinate-swapped position."],"editorial":"Every input cell appears once at its coordinate-swapped position.","tests":[{"id":"lc-867-1","arguments":[[[1,2,3],[4,5,6],[7,8,9]]],"expected":[[1,4,7],[2,5,8],[3,6,9]],"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Rows become the three output columns.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-867-2","argumen